.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_OP_INPUT_NEXT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_op_input_next ,
.Nm dtfl_op_input_cap ,
.Nm dtfl_op_input_cap_delayed ,
.Nm dtfl_op_frontier ,
.Nm dtfl_op_frontier_less_equal ,
.Nm dtfl_op_frontier_less_than ,
.Nm dtfl_op_session ,
.Nm dtfl_op_initial_cap ,
.Nm dtfl_op_scope ,
.Nm dtfl_op_inputs ,
.Nm dtfl_op_outputs ,
.Nm dtfl_op_activator ,
.Nm dtfl_op_sync_activator ,
.Nm dtfl_session_give ,
.Nm dtfl_session_give_message ,
.Nm dtfl_session_close
.Nd operate on an operator's inputs and outputs inside logic
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft dtfl_message *
.Fn dtfl_op_input_next "dtfl_op *op" "size_t input"
.Ft dtfl_cap *
.Fn dtfl_op_input_cap "dtfl_op *op" "size_t input" "size_t output"
.Ft dtfl_cap *
.Fn dtfl_op_input_cap_delayed "dtfl_op *op" "size_t input" "size_t output" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft "const uint64_t *"
.Fn dtfl_op_frontier "const dtfl_op *op" "size_t input" "size_t *n"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_op_frontier_less_equal "const dtfl_op *op" "size_t input" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_op_frontier_less_than "const dtfl_op *op" "size_t input" "const uint64_t *t"
.Ft dtfl_session *
.Fn dtfl_op_session "dtfl_op *op" "size_t output" "const dtfl_cap *cap"
.Ft dtfl_cap *
.Fn dtfl_op_initial_cap "dtfl_op *op" "size_t output"
.Ft dtfl_scope *
.Fn dtfl_op_scope "const dtfl_op *op"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_op_inputs "const dtfl_op *op"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_op_outputs "const dtfl_op *op"
.Ft dtfl_activator *
.Fn dtfl_op_activator "dtfl_op *op"
.Ft dtfl_sync_activator *
.Fn dtfl_op_sync_activator "dtfl_op *op"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_session_give "dtfl_session *s" "const void *rec" "size_t len"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_session_give_message "dtfl_session *s" "const dtfl_message *m"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_session_close "dtfl_session *s"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Fn dtfl_logic_fn
runs with an operator handle
.Fa op
valid only during the call
.Pq Xr dtfl_op_builder_new 3 .
These functions act through it.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_input_next
returns the next message on
.Fa input ,
or
.Dv NULL
when none remain.
The message is valid until the next
.Fn dtfl_op_input_next
call on the same input or until the logic returns; its records are
consumed, for progress tracking, when it is released.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_input_cap
returns a capability on
.Fa output
for the current message's time
.Pq InputCapability retain ,
and
.Fn dtfl_op_input_cap_delayed
one for a later
.Fa t ,
if the summary from
.Fa input
to
.Fa output
reaches it.
Both return a capability the caller owns and must drop
.Pq Xr dtfl_cap_delayed 3 .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_frontier
returns the input's frontier as an antichain of
.Fa *n
times.
.Fn dtfl_op_frontier_less_equal
and
.Fn dtfl_op_frontier_less_than
report whether some frontier element is at or before
.Fa t .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_session
opens an output session on
.Fa output
at
.Fa cap Ns 's
time;
.Fn dtfl_session_give
appends one record,
.Fn dtfl_session_give_message
every record of a received message, and
.Fn dtfl_session_close
flushes and releases the session.
Using a capability not minted for the session's output is a contract
violation and panics
.Pq Xr dtfl_set_panic_hook 3 .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_initial_cap
returns the output's initial capability, at the minimum time, on the
first logic call only; the caller takes ownership and must drop it.
It returns
.Dv NULL
on later calls or once taken.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_scope ,
.Fn dtfl_op_inputs
and
.Fn dtfl_op_outputs
report the operator's scope and port counts.
.Fn dtfl_op_activator
and
.Fn dtfl_op_sync_activator
return activators for the operator
.Pq Xr dtfl_activator_activate 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_op_input_next
returns a borrowed message or
.Dv NULL .
.Fn dtfl_op_input_cap ,
.Fn dtfl_op_input_cap_delayed
and
.Fn dtfl_op_initial_cap
return owned capabilities, the last
.Dv NULL
when unavailable.
.Fn dtfl_op_session
returns a session the caller closes.
.Fn dtfl_op_frontier
returns the frontier times and stores their count in
.Fa *n .
.Sh EXAMPLES
See
.Xr dtfl_op_builder_new 3
for a map operator that reads each input message and gives each record
at the input capability's time.
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
An invalid capability, an output port out of range, or a delay to a time
the summary cannot reach is a contract violation that reaches the panic
hook.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_activator_activate 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_cap_delayed 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_op_builder_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_scope 3
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt InputHandle ,
.Vt OutputHandle ,
.Vt Session
and
.Vt OperatorInfo
.Pq handles.rs , operator_info.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The operator handle, the messages it yields and the sessions it opens
belong to the worker thread running the logic and must not be shared or
outlive the call.
.Fn dtfl_op_sync_activator
returns the one handle that may cross threads.
